              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bob Greenhalgh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making these peas for years without the sugar.(I'm diabetic). I mash the peas, mint and onions in the pot with an immersion blender. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-28T14:05:47.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved the peas. I used a food processor to mash. I also added low-fat milk after combining all other ingredients to add more moisture and a more creamy look and taste.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-06T16:32:04.057Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cocochan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought I'd try this as a change to my usual preparation. It is good but has calories that I can live without. I usually boil peas in a vegetable broth and then use an immersion blender to break down the peas but not to the point that they are completely smooth, but rather chunky. It is comfort food and I eat it as a pick-me-up snack - simple food that is delicious and high in protein too - 1 cup of peas (pre-blended) has more protein than 1 egg (8.6 g vs 6.3 g).",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-08T16:46:47.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MaryLou"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These mashed peas were really yummy. We loved the freshness from the herbs. They were great along side our salmon dish. They were nice, light and sweet. Next time I make them I will leave out the brown sugar, or cut back the amount due to my flavor preference. Definitely use an immersion blender!",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-22T19:20:12.661Z"
          },
          {
